        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under aerobic conditions at room temperature, Gd(NO3)3·6H2O (0.0456 g, 0.1 mmol), CoCl2·6H2O (0.0475 g, 0.2 mmol), H2L ligand (1 mL, 0.2 mmol), pdmH2 (0.0276 g, 0.2 mmol), and triethylamine (0.0810 g, 0.8 mmol) were dissolved in CH3CN (15 mL) and stirred at room temperature for 30 min. The brown, clear solution was filtered, and the filtrate was sealed and naturally evaporated at room temperature. Gray-violet crystals suitable for single-crystal X-ray diffraction were obtained after 3 days, washed with CH3CN, and dried in air.",
